    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">JSC301m · Assessment 2/4</span>\n<h2>Group presentations</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13947 · assessment table (verbatim)</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">JSC301m · Đầu điểm 2/4</span>\n<h2>Group presentations</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13947 · bảng đánh giá (nguyên văn)</p></div>\n<div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type / Loại</span><span class=\"v\">on-going</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Weight / Trọng số</span><span class=\"v\">20.0%</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Parts / Số phần</span><span class=\"v\">1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Completion criteria / Điều kiện hoàn thành</span><span class=\"v\">&gt;0</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Duration / Thời lượng</span><span class=\"v\">20'</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">CLO</span><span class=\"v\">LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Question type / Dạng câu hỏi</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: Essay and multiple-choice questions.<br>Option 2: (Only for Assessment Methods): Follow the instructor’s suggestions</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">No. of questions / Số câu</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: In-class presentations using PPT<br>Option 2: (Only for Assessment Methods): Follow the instructor’s suggestions</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Knowledge &amp; skill / Kiến thức &amp; kỹ năng</span><span class=\"v\">1) Presentation content: Choose a topic from the main textbook.<br>2) May combine online materials and other resources listed in the references to gain deeper understanding of the chosen topic.<br>*Report research results or creative activities in groups (slots 25–29)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Grading guide / Hướng dẫn chấm</span><span class=\"v\">1) The instructor guides students in choosing presentation topics.<br>2) Students form groups of 2–3 people, select a presentation topic, and research additional knowledge related to the chosen topic on the internet or other resources.<br>3) Students prepare slides and get ready to present.<br>4) On presentation day: students take charge of the class. Grades will be based on the following criteria: presentation, debate (asking and answering questions), and contributing feedback to other groups.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Note / Ghi chú</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1:<br><br>1. Presentation content must relate to knowledge about Japanese culture, country, and people.<br>2. The instructor encourages students to present in Japanese and include real-life experiential activities (e.g., cooking, games, Yosakoi dance, wearing kimono, tea ceremony, etc.).<br>3. Students take initiative in creating slides and, if possible, designing engaging experiential activities to present/perform in class.<br>4. ST1: LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4<br>5. ST2: LO5, LO6<br>6. ST3: LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9<br><br>*Duration:<br>Option 2:<br>(Only for Assessment Methods): Follow the instructor’s suggestions<br><br>Option 1: 20'<br>Option 2: (Only for Assessment Methods): Follow the instructor’s guidance</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Sessions in the plan that mention it</h3>\n<ul><li>Session 49 — Students’ presentations or creative/experiential activities: 1–2 groups. Can be carried out in two ways:</li><li>Session 50 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 51 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 52 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 53 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 54 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 55 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 56 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 57 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Session 58 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Buổi trong kế hoạch có nhắc tới</h3>\n<ul><li>Buổi 49 — Students’ presentations or creative/experiential activities: 1–2 groups. Can be carried out in two ways:</li><li>Buổi 50 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 51 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 52 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 53 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 54 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 55 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 56 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 57 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li><li>Buổi 58 — Students’ presentations / creative and experiential activities: 1–2 groups.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">No practice paper for this subject in the Exam Room yet.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">Phòng thi chưa có đề luyện cho môn này.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Exam-strategy notes and worked past papers: coming later.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Chiến lược làm bài và chữa đề: sẽ bổ sung sau.</div></div>"
